## Mandatory Policies

Always load and apply these policies:

- `.ai/agents-core/policies/ddd.md` — DDD rules, Ubiquitous Language, building blocks
- `.ai/agents-core/policies/architecture.md` — Hexagonal + Screaming Architecture
- `.ai/agents-core/policies/testing.md` — Behavior-first testing
- `.ai/agents-core/policies/commits-and-comments.md` — Commits and code comments

---

## Context Loading Order

Load context in this order (later entries override earlier ones):

1. `.ai/agents-core/policies/` — shared DDD and architecture rules
2. `.ai/agents-core/workflow.md` — orchestration protocol and gates
3. `.ai/local/` — local repo overrides (bounded context, UL, thresholds, constraints)

**Local overrides always win.**

---

## Workflow Summary

```
G0 plan → G1 behaviors → DEV-FS → G2 check → REVIEW → G3 verdict
```

- The human decides at G0, G1 and G3. The rest runs without a stop.
- Parallel work only for independent gestures (no shared aggregate).
- The Architect has final authority and asks the human only for blocking doubts after G1.
- DEV-FS makes one commit per gesture (`feat(<ticket>): <behavior>`), never pushes.
- DDD book: use the `ddd` MCP server if available, else `einvoicing-documentation/agents/mcp/ddd/sections/`.

---

## Local Overrides

If `.ai/local/` exists in this repo, apply its content with higher priority than shared rules.

Expected files:

| File | Overrides |
|------|----------|
| `.ai/local/context.md` | Bounded context definition, tech stack |
| `.ai/local/ubiquitous-language.md` | Repo-specific domain glossary |
| `.ai/local/coverage-thresholds.md` | Line coverage targets |
| `.ai/local/constraints.md` | Additional architectural constraints |

---

## Code and Language Rules

- All code, tests, documentation, and agent outputs must be in **English**.
- All domain terms in code must use the Ubiquitous Language verbatim (no translation to technical synonyms).
- Conversational exchanges with the user may remain in French.
